# Large alpha-strike railgun: brutal single hits at sniper reach, with a capacitor
# spike per shot that forces deliberate timing. Fast, tough slugs are hard for
# point-defense to stop.
id          longlance_rail
name        "Long-Lance Railgun"
kind        ballistic
size        L
icon        ic-cannon
damage      45
fire_rate   0.8
proj_speed  16000
# Uniform 0.15 range compression (see autocannon_mk1): 24 -> 3.6s, 384,000 -> 57,600 units.
# Still the longest ballistic reach in the catalog, and now the only one that reaches past
# what the arena look frames -- which is the right shape for the sniper.
proj_life   3.6
proj_radius 5.0
cap_cost    18
emission    0.8
proj_hp     1.6
price       1400
tier        2

# The one def in the catalog that opts out of its kind's default visual family. A rail-driven
# slug is not a propellant round: the launch is an electromagnetic snap with no expanding gas,
# and the shot is a long thin very bright line rather than a short hot streak. Everything else
# ballistic keeps `shell`, which is why this is one authored line and not a code branch.
vfx_family  slug
desc "An alpha-strike railgun for captains who pick their moment. Each slug spikes the capacitor hard - time the shot, or drift powerless."
